th":100,"height":100}}],"accessibility":[{"text":"God decides to bring about the existence of contingent things","targetRectangle":{"y":-314.59115600585938,"x":409.98745456000455,"width":167.03027343750006,"height":95.200001001358032}},{"text":"If it is necessary, then, again, premise (1) of our initial argument is false.","targetRectangle":{"y":-76.32305908203125,"x":228.40013122558594,"width":575.5126953125,"height":64}},{"text":"And if it is contingent, then by the PSR it must have some explanation. But what could this be?","targetRectangle":{"y":14.3072509765625,"x":227.67330932617188,"width":627.18505859375,"height":64}},{"text":"The right hand side of the dilemma might not look too bad at first. We might think, for example, that we can explain God’s creation of contingent things in terms of God’s deciding to create contingent things. ","targetRectangle":{"y":-615.5938720703125,"x":215.17359924316406,"width":564.9658203125,"height":128}},{"text":"Leibniz’s argument","targetRectangle":{"y":99.072799682617188,"x":36.849247805195461,"width":40.913085823141188,"height":26}},{"text":"But this just gives us a new fact:","targetRectangle":{"y":-440.963623046875,"x":320.82545471191406,"width":345.34912109375,"height":32}},{"text":"the","targetRectangle":{"y":25.480010986328125,"x":49.871708560159078,"width":13.212890625,"height":13}},{"text":"PSR","targetRectangle":{"y":38.480010986328125,"x":47.281376806803429,"width":18.393554687499993,"height":13}},{"text":"objections to the ","targetRectangle":{"y":176.60308837890625,"x":21.033818363544995,"width":76.54150390625,"height":42}},{"text":"PSR","targetRectangle":{"y":218.60308837890625,"x":40.843632086658161,"width":31.26904296875,"height":21}},{"text":"And this fact must be necessary, or contingent.","targetRectangle":{"y":-134.953369140625,"x":247.10107421875,"width":492.7978515625,"height":32}}],"baseLayer":{"animations":[],"initialState":{"affineTransform":[1,0,0,1,0,0],"masksToBounds":false,"rotation":0,"scale":1,"